# OpenAPI regeneration policy

`apps/job-service/openapi.json` is a **derived artifact**, produced from NestJS controllers, DTOs, and Swagger decorators (`@ApiProperty`, `@ApiOperation`, `@ApiResponse`, `@ApiTags`, route methods, `class-validator` constraints) by `apps/job-service/scripts/generate-openapi.ts`. Per ADR-0004 the JSON file is the checked-in contract; the decorators are the source-of-truth.

## Regenerate **only when the change set is stable**

Do **not** regenerate after every controller/DTO tweak inside an iteration. Regenerate once, at the end of the work stream, when at least one of these holds:

- The user signals completion (e.g. "commit", "push", "done", "ready", "wrap up", "finish stage N").
- A todo or roadmap stage is being marked done.
- You are about to hand the change off (PR description, manual test instructions, demo).
- The user explicitly asks to update the spec or sync Postman.

Reason: every regeneration produces a noisy JSON diff and triggers a downstream Postman sync — batching keeps reviews and Postman state clean.

## What counts as an OpenAPI-affecting change

Touching any of these inside `apps/job-service/` may shift the spec, so the deferred regeneration becomes mandatory before the change set lands:

- Controllers — route paths, HTTP verbs, `@Controller`, `setGlobalPrefix` / `exclude`.
- DTOs or any class with `@ApiProperty`, `class-validator`, or `class-transformer` decorators.
- Module wiring that adds or removes a controller from the application graph.
- `DocumentBuilder` configuration in `src/main.ts` and `scripts/generate-openapi.ts`.

If a change clearly does not affect any of the above (service body, repository SQL, internal helpers, tests, README), no regeneration is required.

## How to regenerate

```bash
pnpm api:openapi      # writes apps/job-service/openapi.json
pnpm format:fix       # prettier-normalize the JSON before commit
```

Once `apps/job-service/openapi.json` is updated on disk, the steps in `postman-sync.mdc` take over and push the spec to Postman.

## Don't

- Don't regenerate after each save during an iterative refactor.
- Don't hand-edit `openapi.json` — it will be overwritten.
- Don't commit a stale `openapi.json` once the change set is stable; CI is expected to detect drift.
